Built a dynamic 3D Systemic Contagion Surface using rolling market data to visualize how cross-asset stress evolves through time.

Instead of looking at correlations or vol in isolation, I modeled contagion as an evolving interaction energy surface across assets where peaks represent concentrated systemic pressure and valleys represent dispersion.

Each frame shows how strongly assets are moving together. Tall peaks mean stress is building in certain areas of the market. 

What’s interesting is how stress doesn’t rise uniformly, it localizes, spreads, collapses, then reforms, something you can’t see from a simple correlation table.
